# The refraction listing and the match trace (fixtures/131_introspection.ds). `refracted` prints [NDBG.4.3]'s listing and
# `trace N` [NDBG.4.2]'s match trace of the N-th assert's fact; both are reads.
#
#   pump 1   `high` fires for Reading 2, `any` for Readings 1 and 2: three
#            entries, `high`'s first (terminal ordinal, [LDET.5.4])
#   trace    Reading 1 (level 10) is filtered by `high`'s alpha and passes
#            `any`'s; Reading 2 (level 90) passes both. Node ids are the
#            artefact's, so they are compared
#   pump 2   after an unrelated Noise: still three entries -- an unrelated
#            assert and a pump boundary remove nothing ([IRET.11.3.2])
#   pump 3   after retracting Reading 2: its two entries went with its
#            activations, and Reading 1's `any` entry is all that is left
# @spec [NDBG.4.2] [NDBG.4.3]
assert Reading id=1 level=10
assert Reading id=2 level=90
pump
refracted
trace 0
trace 1
assert Noise id=1
pump
refracted
retract 1
pump
refracted
